From dbda2f3461f1a4d7dba793eb916731b5fada4462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:59:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] camera: Propagate GraphicBuffer mapping failures

Avoid shadowing the status returned by GraphicBuffer::lockAsync. Callers must receive mapping errors instead of proceeding with an invalid destination pointer. Source reviewed; Android compilation and runtime tests are deferred to the combined rothko candidate.

Change-Id: Ica8bcd0eb0bc8602fa9290af28487fd939294a35
---
 .../camera/libcameraservice/device3/Camera3StreamInterface.h    | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/camera/libcameraservice/device3/Camera3StreamInterface.h b/services/camera/libcameraservice/device3/Camera3StreamInterface.h
index f07eb3cf03ce5610ac2158c9b9661aef5676822b..fbd7c5012d4ce308d4e853a7229b0294c078d867 100644
--- a/services/camera/libcameraservice/device3/Camera3StreamInterface.h
+++ b/services/camera/libcameraservice/device3/Camera3StreamInterface.h
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@ public:
 
         status_t res = OK;
         if (!_locked) {
-            status_t res =  _buffer->lockAsync(usage, dstBuffer, fenceFd);
+            res = _buffer->lockAsync(usage, dstBuffer, fenceFd);
             if (res == OK) {
                 _locked = true;
             }

From cbd13a24c5124405aee877e21ec4e891812a1387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:10:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] camera: Add per-device opt-in to API3 JPEG_R
 composition

Keep native JPEG_R as the default. For selected provider IDs, derive metadata from real JPEG/P010 capabilities and require concurrent SDR JPEG plus HLG P010. Validate mapped layout and range, preserve the HAL JPEG as the SDR intent, and clean up output buffers on failures.

Source audit and diff checks completed. Test sources cover capability derivation, atomic failure, whole-token selection and range validation. Compilation, test execution and real HAL session/visual validation are deferred to the requested combined candidate. No device opt-in is enabled by this commit.

