From e5e04617427d644cb65f3c8c8e5980c68c443aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:40:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] camera: preserve legacy window tokens in the rothko
 vendor client

The stock face HAL passes AImageReader HIDL native-handle tokens to
ACaptureSessionOutput_create and ACameraOutputTarget_create. Treating
these as ANativeWindow pointers crashes in configureStreamsLocked.

Restore the pre-migration handle types and content comparisons only
for libcamera2ndk_vendor_rothko. Send them through the existing AIDL
windowHandles field supported by the camera service. Keep the V3 client
and its existing isolated graphics dependency graph. Own copied tokens
until lost-buffer callback messages are released, including cancellation.
All other NDK/vendor clients retain the current Surface/ANativeWindow ABI.

Validation: all six affected C++ translation units pass existing target
compiler flags with -fsyntax-only, with and without the private macro.
Device enrollment/authentication still requires the unified build test.

